Apple Inc. (AAPL) released its 10-Q filing after the bell on Wednesday, disclosing a share count of 4.83 billion as of July 20. The updated share count gives Apple a market capitalization of $973.2 billion, using Wednesday's closing price of $201.50. For the company to reach a market capitalization of $1 trillion, Apple shares would have to cross $207. Apple shares were little changed in after-hours trading, after rising 5.9% in Wednesday's session. The company reported better-than-expected results (http://www.marketwatch.com/story/apple-path-to-1-trillion-accelerates-as-consumers-flock-to-pricey-iphones-2018-08-01) for its fiscal third quarter on Tuesday afternoon.
-Emily Bary;
 1653ET
